Two things that matter more than the course list:

The certificate only issues if you complete graded assignments, not just watch. All three have real assignments — budget time for them, not just video-watching time.

Set a cancellation reminder for day 6 or 7 if you don't plan to keep paying — Coursera charges automatically when the trial ends, and refund policies on that first charge are inconsistent depending on which source you check.

If you finish early and want a fourth: Edureka's "Generative AI and LLM Security" (~10 hrs) is the most direct hit on Level 6 — prompt injection, jailbreaks, guardrails — which lines up with the safety test cases in your Month 4 stretch project. I left it out of the core three only because Edureka's brand carries less weight on a resume than Google/Vanderbilt/DeepLearning.AI, not because the content's weaker.

